{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 2 — fix landed for review as Gerrit change **1421**\n\nCommit `e40fca0d9a` -> amended, rebased onto `gerrit/main` 9289fb4b79 locally (main moved\ntwice during this session; rebased both times rather than letting Gerrit do it server-side).\n\n### The fix\n\nThe capability guard 9790 wanted is **kept and relocated**, not deleted:\n- `wait_for_jira_dc_ready` keeps stage 1 (`serverInfo`) byte-for-byte and no longer reads\n  `/rest/api/2/field` at all. The Epic fields are not a session-start property of the instance.\n- `_assert_project_capabilities` — which already runs immediately after\n  `_create_scratch_project`, the first moment the fields can exist — becomes the ONLY Epic-field\n  wait, still bounded, still `AssertionError` on absence, still dumping the inventory.\n  Its `_CAPABILITY_FIELD_CONFIRM_BUDGET_S = 15.0` `min(...)` cap is deleted because its stated\n  premise ('readiness already waited out the full field budget at session start') is now false.\n- `scripts/jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe.py`: project create now precedes `_await_named_fields`.\n  Both tiers still route through the one shared `await_required_fields`.\n- `not_ready_message` rewritten — the words 'budget' and 'JIRA_DC_FIELD_READY_TIMEOUT' no\n  longer appear in it; it names the provisioning precondition and says outright that waiting\n  cannot help.\n- `FIELD_READY_BUDGET_S` 600 -> **120**, attributable at last to\n  `PROVISIONING_TO_FIELDS_VISIBLE_S = 0.0512` (run 30981084637) — ~2400x headroom, still bounded,\n  so a genuine degrade fails in two minutes rather than ten. Poll cadence 10s -> 1s because the\n  quantity waited on is sub-second now, not multi-minute. A successful wait finally records its\n  elapsed time (shared `ready_message`), so a green run stops discarding the only datapoint an\n  allowance can be sized from.\n\n### RED -> GREEN, held out\n\nThe fix was written by a subagent that never saw the tests: the test file was moved OUT of its\ntree and declared off-limits, and it was given only the proven mechanism plus a contract card.\n\nRED first, against unmodified source (4 cells, each for its own reason):\n| cell | pre-fix failure |\n|---|---|\n| `..._tolerates_the_pre_provisioning_inventory` | `RuntimeError: required Epic field(s) ...` |\n| `..._does_not_gate_on_the_epic_fields_at_all` | same — session start still polls `/field` |\n| `..._does_not_send_the_reader_at_the_budget` | 'the failure still points the reader at the readiness budget' |\n| `..._probe_creates_its_project_before_it_awaits_the_epic_fields` | order `['await-fields', ...]` |\n\nThen **21 passed** against that held-out oracle.\n\nOne honest note on process: the probe-ordering cell first failed for a TEST reason (its fake\nHTTP layer did not model the probe's idempotent project DELETE, so it raised before recording\nanything). The fix was **reverted out** first, the test corrected, re-verified RED with no fix\npresent, and only then was the fix re-applied — never edited together.\n\n### Mutation checks (fix perturbed; every cell must return RED)\n\n| mutation | result |\n|---|---|\n| session-start field gate restored (the deadlock itself) | 2 cells RED |\n| the wait degraded to a one-shot read | `..._capability_check_waits...` RED |\n| 'budget' blame put back into the failure prose | `..._does_not_send_the_reader...` RED |\n| probe's original ordering restored | `..._probe_creates_its_project...` RED |\n| `ready=True` on expiry (the blindness 9790 removed) | degrade + unreadable cells RED, DID NOT RAISE |\n\nFix restored byte-identical after each (`diff` clean), 21 passed.\n\n### Fix-safety audit\n\n- **Restoration, not creation** — no new entry point, command or user-visible artifact; the\n  change removes a gate and moves a check that already existed.\n- **No new dependency** — the only added imports are stdlib `importlib.util`/`pathlib` inside a\n  test function. `jira_dc_field_readiness.py` remains standard-library-only, as its workflow\n  requires.\n- **No test weakening** — no `skip`/`xfail` added, no assertion loosened. Five cells were\n  removed and six added; every removed cell encoded the REFUTED premise (that the Epic fields\n  are a session-start predicate) and each one's real invariant survives at the corrected call\n  site.\n\nGates: `make lint` **0**, `make typecheck` **0** (434 files). Live verification run\n**30982731669** in flight."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785913407590263001,"uuid":"967bf15c-e99a-4442-96ea-034f891ab6ac"}